ECHO - show text, echo batch lines››Syntax:› ECHO ON|OFF› ECHO [/N] text››ECHO ON makes the command processor›show each command line it runs, also›from batch files; ECHO OFF (the›default) stops it.››ECHO text writes the text; variables›like $PATH are replaced by their›values. Output can be redirected.››Options:› /N  no end of line after the text››Examples:› ECHO Hello› ECHO $PATH› ECHO TEXT >>D1:FILE.TXT›